<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-base"><div class="border border-ink p-3"><strong>Filling</strong><p>A finite amount of ideal liquid.</p></div><div class="border border-ink p-3"><strong>Same-thickness coat</strong><p>Would need infinite paint.</p></div></div>
<figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">This is a schematic of the mathematical shape. A layer allowed to get thinner without limit can touch the entire wall using finite volume. A coating of fixed positive thickness cannot. Real paint cannot reach arbitrarily far inside.</figcaption>
